## **Important String Methods**
| **Method** | **Description** |
|------------|----------------|
| `length()` | Returns string length |
| `charAt(index)` | Returns character at a given index |
| `substring(start, end)` | Returns a substring |
| `contains("text")` | Checks if a substring exists |
| `toLowerCase()` | Converts to lowercase |
| `toUpperCase()` | Converts to uppercase |
| `trim()` | Removes leading/trailing spaces |
| `replace(old, new)` | Replaces characters |
| `split(delimiter)` | Splits a string into an array |
| `equals(str)` | Checks if two strings are equal |
| `equalsIgnoreCase(str)` | Checks equality ignoring case |
| `concat(str)` | Joins two strings |

---

## **String Example Code in Java**
```java
public class Main {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        String str = "Hello, Java!";
        
        // Length of string
        System.out.println("Length: " + str.length()); // Output: 12

        // Character at index 1
        System.out.println("Char at 1: " + str.charAt(1)); // Output: e

        // Substring from index 7
        System.out.println("Substring: " + str.substring(7)); // Output: Java!

        // Convert to uppercase
        System.out.println("Uppercase: " + str.toUpperCase()); // Output: HELLO, JAVA!

        // Replace a character
        System.out.println("Replace: " + str.replace("Java", "World")); // Output: Hello, World!
    }
}
```

